{"sections":[{"type":"Header","title":"Employment, unemployment and economic inactivity in Carlisle","label":"How Carlisle compares with the North West and Great Britain across employment-related statistics"},{"id":"mainlines","type":"Summary","title":"in Carlisle:","content":"<a name=\"section-top\"></a>","sections":[{"indicator":"Employment rate","value":"78.2%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Employment in Carlisle has decreased since compared with the previous year</p><p><a href=\"#section-employment\">Go to employment rate section</a></p>"},{"indicator":"Unemployment rate","value":"3.6%","age_band":"(ages 16+)","content":"<p>The unemployment rate in Carlisle was 3.6% in the year ending March 2023.</p><p><a href=\"#section-unemployment\">Go to unemployment rate section</a></p>"},{"indicator":"Claimant Count","value":"2.6%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Claimant Count was lower in the year ending July 2023 than a year earlier. Claimant Count measures the number of people who are <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/aguidetolabourmarketstatistics#claimant-count\">claiming unemployment-related benefits.</a>  </p><p><a href=\"#section-claimant\">Go to Claimant Count section</a>  </p>"},{"indicator":"Economic inactivity","value":"2.6%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Economic inactivity has increased since the previous year. These are people who are neither employed nor seeking work.</p><p><a href=\"#section-inactive\">Go to economic inactivity section</a></p>"}]},{"type":"Caveat","content":"<p>All estimates are based on the <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/surveys/informationforhouseholdsandindividuals/householdandindividualsurveys/labourforcesurvey\"> Labour Force Survey</a>. Data for local areas are based on smaller sample sizes than national figures and may vary more year to year.</p>"},{"type":"Employment_rate","content":"<a name=\"section-employment\"></a><h2>Employment in Carlisle has decreased compared with the previous year</h2><p>Carlisle's employment rate was higher than across the North West as a whole in the year ending March 2023.</p><p>Of people aged 16 to 64 years living in Carlisle, 78.2% were employed in the year ending March 2023. This is a decrease compared with the year ending March 2022 when the local rate was 83.3%.</p><p>Across the North West in the year ending  March 2023, 73.6% of people aged 16 to 64 years were employed. This was higher compared with the previous year, when 73.1% of people were employed.</p>"},{"id":"chart-timeseries","type":"Chart","chartType":"line-highlight","title":"Employment rate in the North West among those aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending 2012 to year ending March 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"z":"Manchester","x":"2012","y":58.8},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2013","y":61.2},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2014","y":62.1},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2015","y":62.4},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2016","y":63.9},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2017","y":62.9},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2018","y":68.9},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2019","y":68.8},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2020","y":66.5},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2021","y":69},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2022","y":68.1},{"z":"Manchester","x":"2023","y":68.2},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2012","y":72.9},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2013","y":63.7},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2014","y":67.1},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2015","y":68.2},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2016","y":71.6},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2017","y":80.3},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2018","y":76.7},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2019","y":71.1},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2020","y":67.9},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2021","y":78.4},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2022","y":72.2},{"z":"Lancaster","x":"2023","y":75.9},{"z":"Preston","x":"2012","y":68.1},{"z":"Preston","x":"2013","y":68.4},{"z":"Preston","x":"2014","y":69.9},{"z":"Preston","x":"2015","y":66.4},{"z":"Preston","x":"2016","y":69.4},{"z":"Preston","x":"20