us four weeks or were unable to start work within the next two weeks. Common reasons include being retired, looking after the home or family or being temporarily or long-term sick and disabled.</p><p>Economic inactivity in Carlisle is lower than across the North West and Great Britain.</p><p>Across the North West, 23.5% of people aged 16 to 64 years were economically inactive during the year ending  2022, an increase compared with the same period in March 2022 when 23.4% were economically inactive.</p><p>Overall in Great Britain, 21.6% of people aged 16 to 64 years were economically inactive, compared with 21.5% in the same period of March 2022.</p>"},{"id":"chart-inactivity","type":"Chart","chartType":"bar","title":"Highest economic inactivity rates in the North West, residents aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending March 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"x":32.2,"y":"Wyre"},{"x":30.3,"y":"Chorley"},{"x":30.2,"y":"Rochdale"},{"x":29.4,"y":"Barrow-in-Furness"},{"x":29.4,"y":"Pendle"}],"padding-left":"160"},{"type":"end","content":"<p><a href=\"#section-top\">Back to top</a></p>"},{"type":"Nomis","content":"<h2>More data on the Carlisle labour market </h2><p>You can view and download more data on the labour market on the <a href=\"https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/reports/lmp/la/1946157077/report.aspx\">Carlisle area profile page on Nomis.</a>  </p>"},{"type":"About","content":"<h2>About the data</h2><p>The content in this article is generated using semi-automated journalism, based on rules pre-programmed by Office for National Statistics (ONS) staff.</p><p>This is a new product in Beta release, intended to improve the accessibility of labour market data to local authority level. Leave us feedback. </p>"}],"place":{"areacd":"E07000028","areanm":"Carlisle","geography":"Non-metropolitan District","parentcd":"E12000002","parentnm":"North West","total_authorities":39,"supergroupnm":"Services and Industrial Legacy",